                <pb facs="0756" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860n.00/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-09T15:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 9—2:52
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>99. In view of general situation Baltic Provinces I strongly urge American naval
                    vessel, preferably destroyer, be despatched Baltic waters. This recommendation
                    concurred in by military attache [is made] only after most careful study and
                    consideration of entire situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
